      "math_academy_id": "e-816",
      "problem": "What is $\\textrm{GCF}(10k,20)?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the GCF, we list the factors of the coefficients and identify any common variable factors in the expressions.\n\nThe factors of $10$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\quad 2,\\quad 5,\\quad 10.\n$$\n\nThe factors of $20$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\quad 2,\\quad 4,\\quad 5,\\quad 10,\\quad 20.\n$$\n\nThe common factors of $10$ and $20$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\quad 2,\\quad 5,\\quad 10.\n$$\n\nThe greatest of these common factors is $10.$\n\nNow we look at the variable factors. Since $20$ has no variable and $10k$ contains $k,$ there are no variable factors in common.\n\nThus, $\\textrm{GCF}(10k,20)=10.$",
